From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:27:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: jpeg: baseline JPEG encoder for T8140

Turn the JPEG scaffold into a V4L2 memory-to-memory encoder for the A18
Pro (T8140) engines. It takes full-range NV12M (4:2:0) or NV16M (4:2:2)
frames and produces baseline JPEG with the standard Huffman tables, at a
quality set by V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY (Annex K tables with the
libjpeg scaling) and an optional restart interval.

T8140 widens every DMA address to a 64-bit low/high pair, which moves the
colour, input-format, timeout and revision registers up from the m1n1
map. The engine is identified by its revision with the stepping ignored,
reset with the documented handshake before every job, and programmed
with one ordered register list that KUnit checks write by write. The
interrupt is acknowledged in the engine's order: completion status, run
bit, prefetch and mask. Registers past the control block are only touched
once MODE has opened them, which is what made early writes fault.

T6041 is still refused: its layout is not supported yet.

Originally-by: Acelogic <miguelc4600@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/linux-aurora/commit/3e77f272d9bb8940de8e744ead8d638e65f7500f
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 6f1281f793d44f44e84b01e6529598fe8e11f91f)
